<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 30 December, from 534 to 2006.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/534">534 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The second edition of the Codex Justinianus takes effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The revised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a>, compiled on the orders of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> and published in November as the Codex Repetitae Praelectionis, came into force. Its twelve books covered ecclesiastical, private, criminal and administrative law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/999">999 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,027 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brian Boru crushes Leinster and Dublin at Glenmama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Probably near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyons</a> Hill in County <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kildare">Kildare</a>, the forces of Munster and Meath under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a> and the High King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mael-sechnaill-mac-domnaill">Máel Sechnaill II</a> crushed the armies of Leinster and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> led by King Máel Mórda, ending the brief Leinster revolt.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1066">1066 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Muslim mob in Granada kills the Jewish vizier Joseph ibn Naghrela</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Muslim mob stormed the royal palace of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, killed the Jewish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> Joseph ibn Naghrela and massacred members of the city's Jewish community.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1460">1460 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">566 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard, Duke of York, is killed at Wakefield</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lancastrian forces defeated and killed Richard, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, near Wakefield. His son Edward avenged him at Towton three months later and took the throne as Edward IV.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1853">1853 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">173 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Gadsden Purchase treaty is signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US minister James Gadsden signed a treaty in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> buying land south of the Gila River for a railway route. It fixed the modern border of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Grigori Rasputin is murdered in Petrograd</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nobles led by Prince Felix Yusupov killed Rasputin, the mystic whose influence over the imperial family had become a scandal (17 December, Old Style). The murder did not save the monarchy, which fell weeks later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grigori-rasputin">Grigori Rasputin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1922">1922 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">104 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union is formally established</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> and the Transcaucasian Federation approved the treaty creating the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics. It lasted until 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2006">2006 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">20 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Saddam Hussein is executed in Baghdad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former Iraqi president was hanged for crimes against humanity over the Dujail killings. A leaked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mobile-phone">mobile phone</a> video of the jeering at his execution caused controversy.</p></div></li></ol>
